A||||19||Cliff Pennock||FDD-X1 Digital Dash resurrected||||1||
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||06-22-2001||03:20 PM||||Because of a <B>very</B> busy work schedule, I had not been actively persuing sales of the FDD-X1 Digital Dash. I had been in contact with some companies that would possibly distribute it in the States (if you guys read this, sorry I never contacted you anymore).<P>As it seems, my schedule is clearing up which means I'll have the time to start producing the dashboards again. It will take a little time because I want to implement a few design changes, but I'll keep you updated.<P>At first, I'll sell directly to the customer. Depending on its success, I'll start talking with the potential distributors again.<P>Price will be somewhere between $500-$750. For those of you who have no idea what I'm talking about, here's a pic of the dash installed in my Fiero. This pic was taken with a very crappy digital cam. The pic doesn't do the dash justice, it looks 1000 times better in real.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Ddash4.jpg"> <P>For more information, click <A HREF="http://www.pennock.nl/fdd-x1.htm" TARGET=_blank>here.</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-22-2001||04:54 PM||||Oh, great!  Now I have to save up my money for something other than suspension parts.  I really wanted to lower my car, too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>What happens to the aux gauges?  Do they stay analog or do you produce digital gauges to replace those?  These are plug 'n play, right?  What design changes do you have in mind?  Will you be selling these to those of us in the States that are still drooling over them?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Too bad I don't already have an online Fiero business.  If I did, I'd be more than willing to be a Stateside distributor.  Hopefully, you'll be able to sell them directly to us over here as I'd be worried about the middleman markup.<P>Keep us informed, Cliff!<P>MM  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||06-22-2001||06:12 PM||||<I>&gt; What happens to the aux gauges?</I><P>I haven't got a digital replacement <I>yet</I>. But since the FDD-X1 has two Aux-In ports, and a Port to update the software, once they are available it's as simple as plugging it in, download new software from the website, and upload this software to the Dash.<P><I>&gt; These are plug 'n play, right?</I><P>Yes, it should install in 15-30 minutes.<P><I>&gt; What design changes do you have in mind?</I><P>It's not a design change, but a software update. The dash already automatically displays 0-60mph times (only when it detects you are really going got it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ), and I want it to be able to display 1/4 mile times too.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||06-22-2001||08:41 PM||||Will I be able to continue to use my stock aux gauges?  What kind of time frame are you looking at for this?  Will you sell to individuals in the US or just the Netherlands?<P>Sorry, but I need info.  All I have to do is talk my wife into getting a second job.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I've thought these were killer since the 1st time I saw them (Nov '99).  Gotta get some!<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||06-22-2001||09:29 PM||||Cliff,I noticed your dash is considerably nicer than the stock dash configuration shown on your web site.Which dash will you be selling,and how do we order one?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bazooka||06-22-2001||10:49 PM||||Cliff, <BR>    That's a great looking dash. It looks like the 'finishing touch' that could be used on any nicely customized vehicle. Will you be offering the display in blue (turquoise or cyan) also? Is the 'speedo' a 120 mph or higher? It would be interesting to have a G-Tech style readout for acceleration and 1/8 or 1/4 mile built in, But without needing to reset the level gauge that they have. How about incorporating a 'mileage calculator' and a vacuum gauge. It does look very promising, and I hope you can market it.<BR> <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html</A> <BR>****************************************<BR>[QUOTE]Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Because of a [b]very</B> busy work schedule, I had not been actively persuing sales of the FDD-X1 Digital Dash.<BR>****************************************<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex2004||06-22-2001||11:15 PM||||Will the digital dash tach work w/ a 4 cyl? That is one awesome digital dash!!!<P>Alex....<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000007||AusFiero||06-23-2001||03:26 AM||||Nice dash Cliff.<BR>If you need a website to market it on give me a yell. I am sure we could fit it into <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>www.auto-alley.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||14
Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||06-23-2001||03:55 AM||||<I>&gt; Will I be able to continue to use my stock aux gauges?</I><P>Yes.<P><I>&gt; Will you sell to individuals in the US or just the Netherlands?</I><P>I will sell it worldwide.<P><I>&gt; Cliff,I noticed your dash is considerably nicer than the stock dash configuration shown on<BR>&gt; your web site.Which dash will you be sellingand how do we order one?</I><P>They are actually one and the same dash with only a few minor cosmetic differences. The dash on <B>this</B> picture uses a custom front plate which I designed myself. The front plate is <B>not</B> included but is very easy to build. Instructions on how to build this front plate yourself <B>are</B> included however. Another difference is the lettering used (The "FUEL" and "TEMP" indicators are larger and they use larger icons).<P><I>&gt; and how do we order one?</I><P>You'll be able to order online. Payment will be PayPal or credit card.<P><I>&gt; Will you be offering the display in blue (turquoise or cyan) also?</I><P>Not yet. The dash uses LED displays and although blue LEDs have just become available, blue LED <I>displays</I> do not yet exist. The blue displays used in VCRs, tvs and some modern car dashes are Vaccuum Fluorescent Displays. You can get different colors however like Green, Yellow and Orange or a combination but let me warn you that that doesn't look as good as plain ol' red.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><I>&gt; Is the 'speedo' a 120 mph or higher?</I><P>The speedo is not limited.<P><I>&gt;How about incorporating a 'mileage calculator' and a vacuum gauge.</I><P>As of yet, I have no plans for either. The mileage calculator would be very inaccurate and would need a flow meter to make it accurate.<P><I>Will the digital dash tach work w/ a 4 cyl?</I><P>Yes. The FDD-X1 uses an on board menu system. You have 3 external buttons to change the settings. So switching from 6 to 4 cylinders is just a matter of a few keypresses. It's just as easy switching from mph to km/h.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Greg Piet||06-23-2001||03:21 PM||||Cliff,<P>I know I have mentioned this before, but since it is being ressurected...<BR>The option to have the oil pressure displayed in the main dash would be a good option, as not everyone has the center rally pod, and the oil pressure gauge in my opinion is an important faeture||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cliff Pennock||06-23-2001||04:43 PM||||Hmmmm. I'll have to look into that. There isn't room for a seperate display for the oil-pressure, but it could be displayed optionally on one of the text displays. However, there's already a lot of electronics as it is in there. I'm not sure if the extra electronics will even fit.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||06-23-2001||06:55 PM||||Greg--You can buy the aux gauges for way less than $100 and install them yourself.  If you're going to spend $500-$750 on Cliffs gauges, surely you can afford another hundred bucks?  Seems to me, if Cliff adds much more to the gauges, the price will jump.  I want to be able to afford them.  Not flaming by any means.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000012||Greg Piet||06-23-2001||08:37 PM||||I hear ya MM...<BR>I dont really like the rally pod to be blunt.<BR>I use the oil pressure and tach more than any other gauges...  In my current setup they are  close to each other..<BR>A quick glance and I have checked both gauges.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Monkeyman||06-24-2001||01:29 AM||||My bad, Greg.  Since I love the aux gauges, I hadn't even thought about someone not liking them.  If there's not enough space to add that to Cliffs "stock" digigauges, what about adding an aftermarket digigauge to your A pillar?  I guess that's probably a stupid idea since you like being able to read everything at once.  Hmmm...Maybe have Dakota Digital make something really low profile for you?  You could mount it to the top of your gauge cluster.  Someone will thing of something.  <P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000014||Alex2004||06-24-2001||04:36 PM||||What all is it going to display such as like the turn signal indicators deck ajar, BRAKE, ect...? Also, would the mileage remain the same?  And is there anyway i could make the mileage what is was on my old instrument cluster?<P>Alex...<P><p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 06-24-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000015||Greg Piet||06-24-2001||06:14 PM||||I know cliff had an extra text window that was not used.  If that could be used to output the oil pressure I would be a happy camper.<BR>Cliff already knows this from his post stating there might not be enough room inside the box...  we will see!<P>To be honest, I absolutely love cliffs setup, and if I already had the rally pod I might like it.  But I am an old stubborn mule.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||Predator||06-25-2001||07:56 AM||||Cliff, Your Digital Dash is the only one I have ever considered buying. I was disappointed when I heard you were not selling them in the US. This is great news. I will start saving now. Let us all know when they go up for sale. Also, I would like a set of digital aux gauges if you decide to make them to match.. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000017||Cliff Pennock||06-25-2001||02:49 PM||||<I>&gt; What all is it going to display such as like the turn signal indicators deck ajar, BRAKE, ect...?</I><P>It uses the standard indicators for that. But... that might change since that's one of the design changes I want to make.<P><I>&gt; Also, would the mileage remain the same?</I><P>Well, it uses the standard odometer. But since I want to ship the dash pre-installed in a standard gauge pod, you'll have to tell me the mileage so I can set the odometer to that. This probably isn't legal, but it's the only way to get it pre-installed.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Greg Piet||06-25-2001||07:13 PM||||I think due to the age of the Fiero, that in most states the Fiero is exempt from odometer readings...<P>This may reduce the legality issue that you brought up.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Monkeyman||06-25-2001||09:04 PM||||I don't know about other states, but in Indiana exempt means that the odometer has rolled over.  Tough to do when the odometer in a Fiero will go to 999,999.  There are however, two other boxes that can be checkmarked.  One says, 'The odometer reading stated is in excess of the mechanical limits' and the other says, 'The odometer reading is NOT actual mileage'.  Seems like the only time you would be in trouble is if you neglected to check the second box if you were to sell the car.  Even then you probably couldn't get in too much trouble as long as the buyer didn't care.  <P>Cliff--My actual mileage is "0".  That's what you can put on my set of digigauges when you make them.  Ooops.  Almost forgot.  I need money 1st.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>MM||||reg||1
